==English==
{{was wotd|2021|August|26}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɹaɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-I learned some phrases-pry.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪ|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
The {{glossary|verb}} is inherited from {{inh|en|enm|prien}}, {{m|enm|pryen|t=to look closely, peer into, pry, spy}}{{nb...|preien, preye, pri, prie, prihe, prye, pryhe|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=prīen|pos=v|id=MED34607}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|*prīwan}}, {{m|ang|*prēowian|t=to look narrowly, to squint at}}, attested by {{cog|ang|beprīwan}}, {{m|ang|beprēwan|t=to wink}}; further etymology unknown,<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=153665|date=December 2020|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|alt=pry{{sup|1}}|pos=v}}</ref> but probably akin to {{cog|ang|*prēowot|t=closing of the eyes}}, attested only in combination&nbsp;– compare {{m|ang|prēowthwīl|t=blink or twinkling of an eye, moment}}, {{m|ang|princ|t=a wink}}: see {{l|en|prink}}.

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from the verb.<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=† pry|pos=''n.''{{sup|3}}|noformat=1|id=153663|date=March 2019}}</ref>

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}}
## To [[peer#Verb|peer]] [[closely]] and [[curiously]], especially at something [[closed#Adjective|closed]] or not [[public#Adjective|public]].
##* {{RQ:Dekker et al Patient Grissell|page=11|lines=293–294|passage=[W]omen haue eagles eyes, / To '''prie''' euen to the heart, and why not you?}}
##* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=VIII|page=232|lines=158–161|passage={{...}} to elude, thus wrapt in miſt / Of midnight vapor glide obſcure, and '''prie''' / In every Buſh and brake, where hap may finde / The Serpent ſleeping, {{...}}|year=1873}}
##* {{RQ:Wordsworth White Doe|page=19|passage=And choice of studious friends had he / Of Bolton's  dear fraternity: / {{...}} / [I]n their cells with him did '''pry''' / For other lore,—through strong desire / Searching the earth with chemic fire: {{...}}}}
## {{lb|en|figuratively}} To [[inquire]] into something that does not [[concern#Verb|concern]] one; to be [[nosy]]; to [[snoop#Verb|snoop]].
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 6-2|act=I|scene=i|page=122|column=1|passage=Watch thou, and wake when others be aſleepe, / To '''prie''' into the ſecrets of the State, {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Forster Room with a View|chapter=Possibilities of a Pleasant Outing|page=73|passage=We literary hacks are shameless creatures. I believe there's no secret of the human heart into which we wouldn't '''pry'''.}}
##: {{usex|en|I don't mean to '''pry''', but could you tell me where you got that scarf?}}
##: {{usex|en|to '''pry''' into someone's affairs}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To peer at (something) closely; also, to [[look into]] (a [[matter]], etc.) [[thoroughly]].
#* {{RQ:Melville White Jacket|chapter=Night and Day Gambling in a Man-of-War|page=357|passage=The two ship's corporals went among the sailors by the names of Leggs and Pounce; {{...}} Bland, the master-at-arms, ravished with their dexterity in '''prying''' out offenders, used to call them his two right hands.}}

